+# The FAA answer in the May hearing record and its earlier testimony source
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01 / PD07. Acquired the archived, annotated May 23 staff print, a two-page hearing schedule draft, and the public May 22 Commission and October 25, 2001 Senate hearing PDFs. The staff print ends before the May 23 FAA statement read-in. Its notes and the public hearing records preserve different descriptions of the earlier notification testimony. [Exact sources and hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Staff print and public transcript boundaries
+
+The Team 8 Box 5 staff print contains **59** physical pages and is filed with notes on Mineta, McKinley, Arnold and Scott. Physical p. 59 ends when Kean calls Canavan. The two held public PDFs have identical bytes and **119** pages, and the same transition appears at p. 59. The report of the FAA statement's receipt and the read-in appear later, at physical **p. 78** lines **15–39**. This comparison identifies the scope of the staff print and the exact later location. The remainder of the staff working copy, if separately filed, remains unlocated. [Public transcript, p. 59](https://www.911commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-23.pdf#page=59) · [Public transcript, p. 78](https://www.911commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-23.pdf#page=78) · [Commission archive package](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip)
+
+For each staff page, I compared sets of exact four-token sequences against all 119 public pages, using sorted embedded text and whitespace tokenization. Each of the 59 staff pages had a unique highest match at the same page number. This tests page alignment. The transcriptions still differ in places, and the paper scan preserves annotations absent from the digital public transcript. Staff p. 28 line 23 extracts **`9~: 2 5`** while its image and the public transcript both show **`9:25`** at that location. These readings remain separately pinned. [Scores and scoped image coordinates](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+Marcus item 492 is a schedule draft. Its two page footers carry **5/14/03** in the embedded layer. Its May 23 morning panel lists Mineta, McKinley and Canavan. The public May 23 transcript's first panel also lists Arnold and Scott. Keep the roster difference by source. The schedule print supplies neither a date of approval nor evidence of receipt of an FAA statement. [Public May 23 transcript, p. 1](https://www.911commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-23.pdf#page=1)
+
+## Earlier testimony and the May request
+
+| Record | Wording or value preserved |
+| --- | --- |
+| **October 25, 2001 Senate Armed Services hearing**, physical p. 21 / printed 18, lines 21–40 | Levin's question gives **9:25**. Eberhart gives **9:24** and qualifies the Department of Defense answer as the first documented notification. [Senate hearing, oral exchange](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-107shrg78817/pdf/CHRG-107shrg78817.pdf#page=21) |
+| **Written follow-up printed in the same Senate volume**, physical p. 51 / printed 48, lines 34–49 | The question again gives **9:25 a.m.** Eberhart gives **0924 EDT**, specifies NEADS receiving notice of a possible hijacking, and repeats the documented-notification qualifier for DOD. This is a written question-and-answer record. The passage alone does not date the actual return. [Senate hearing, written answer](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-107shrg78817/pdf/CHRG-107shrg78817.pdf#page=51) |
+| **May 22, 2003 Commission hearing**, physical p. 119 lines 19–47 | Ben-Veniste identifies the **Senate Armed Services Committee**, October 25, 2001, and Levin. He repeats **9:25** in the question and **9:24** in the reply. Garvey asks to submit an answer for the record because her recollection differs and she wants to check it. [May 22 transcript](https://www.9-11commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-22.pdf#page=119) |
+| **May 23 staff print**, p. 27 lines 37–46 and p. 28 lines 19–39 | The question addressed to McKinley invokes previous **House Armed Services Committee** testimony and then invokes General **Eberhardt**. At p. 28 the question distinguishes **9:25**, **9:24**, documented notification and notification of any type. The handwritten right margin says **“House Armed Services Comm.”**, attributes the account directly to **Eberhart** and says FAA first notified NORAD about AAL 77 at **9:24 A.M.** The handwritten line contains no documented-notification qualifier. |
+| **May 23 public transcript**, physical p. 78 lines 15–39 | Ben-Veniste says Garvey communicated with staff the previous evening and the staff received a statement from FAA. The transcript attributes authorship as reported to him and prints **“Mr. Asmus”**. It reads the FAA's answer referring to **9:24 a.m.** as formal notification, along with its separate claim about earlier bridge communications. [Public transcript, p. 78](https://www.911commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-23.pdf#page=78) |
+
+The Senate volume and May 22 transcript supply a dated source for the distinctive Levin–Eberhart exchange. Retain the House references, the printed **Eberhart** and **Eberhardt** spellings and the different qualifiers as separate observations. The annotation's author, date and exact referent remain uncertain. A House proceeding or briefing that the annotator actually used, the hearing preparer's source packet and dated staff notes could distinguish the attributions. This unit did not establish the underlying operational notice time. [Senate volume](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-107shrg78817/pdf/CHRG-107shrg78817.pdf) · [Public May 23 transcript](https://www.911commission.gov/archive/hearing2/9-11Commission_Hearing_2003-05-23.pdf#page=27)
+
+## Verification and remaining originals
+
+The selected images, six body hashes, two ZIP CRCs, 59 same-number page matches and 30 literal anchor occurrences were checked. The first verifier used the wrong key for a held source manifest and stopped before alignment. Its corrected version used the manifest's actual key. The source records were unchanged. The page comparison screened embedded text across both transcripts and the substantive reading remained focused on the cited passages. Raw scans, visual crops, contact fields and archive webmail parameters stay local.
+
+The May 22 request and May 23 read-in establish the public record of the question and the reported handover. The native cover, attachment, exact date and time of actual Commission intake, and any version after the response was found inaccurate remain open. The signed administrative decision and recommendation-specific outcomes remain priority records. Seek the May 22 evening message and Commission intake copy, the later corrected answer and its dated receipt, and the original source material for the earlier hearing references. [Prior receipt review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2e8a072977f1fd387a2cb9e3e0336e5268a7d895/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-knowledge-correction-trail-2026-10-26/README.md) · [Open records queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
